<P>
<BOX>(<EMPHASIS>(OLB-019\BOLD))
<X>(<BOX>(OLB-019))
Paul Cotton noted the following Possible Problem derived from  WG3:SAF-052R1:

<LIST>(SIMPLE)

<LE>Severity: Major Technical

<LE>Reference: P10

<LE>Source: Paul Cotton, WG3:SAF-052R1

<LE>Description:

<P>
Dynamic SQL and CLI use the descriptor fields SCOPE_CATALOG, SCOPE_SCHEMA
and SCOPE_NAME to describe the scope of a REF column when a DESCRIBE
OUTPUT is specified.  In addition these interfaces permit the scope of 
an input parameter value to be specified in these descriptor fields.

<P>
SAF-052R1 added support to SQL/OLB for references but there is no
mechanism in SQL/OLB to permit an application to determine the scope of 
a REF column or to specify the scope of a REF parameter.


<LE>Proposed Solution:

<P>
An additional setRef method could be added that took an addiitonal
parameter(s) to specify the scope of the supplied REF value.  Some method
of obtaining the scope of a REF value should also be supplied.  Since the
scope is constant for a column this is best returned as part of the
column's metadata.


<ENDLIST>

<ENDCOMMENT>




<COMMENT>===Resolved by WG3:DRS-080/H2-2002-458

