<P>
<BOX>(<EMPHASIS>(OLB-006\BOLD))
<X>(<BOX>(OLB-006))
On the first FCD ballot (1999), comment GBR-P10-013 noted the following
Language Opportunity:

<LIST>(SIMPLE)

<LE>Severity: Language Opportunity

<LE>Reference: P10-03., Introduction

<LE>Source: First FCD ballot, comment GBR-P10-013

<LE>Description:

<P>
Much of the material in clause 3 is of a tutorial nature and inappropriate
for inclusion in a standard.  Other elements provide necessary information,
but are in unusual or inappropriate places compared to the common
placement of such material in other parts of the SQL standard.  The
contents of the clause should be reviewed and either discarded or
relocated, as is appropriate for each element.  In general terms, much of
3.1, Overview, should be discarded, but some is a candidate for inclusion
in a 'Concepts' clause.  'Design goals' are not normally expressed in the
normative parts of a standard, so 3.2, 'Design goals', should be discarded.
In other parts of the SQL standard, conformance requirements are specified
in a separate clause, the final normative clause of each part, so 3.3,
'Conformance' should be relocated to conform to this precedent.  The
comparisons with binding styles for other host languages should be
discarded from 3.5 and 3.6, with the remaining material being considered
for inclusion in a Concepts clause.


<LE>Proposed Solution: None submitted with comment

<ENDLIST>

<ENDCOMMENT>


<COMMENT>===Resolved by WG3:WLG-057/H2-2005-326r1

