<problem>

<para>
SQL/OLB should make it possible for an SQL/OLB application to use the JDBC
3.0 support of what JDBC 3.0 refers to as 'Auto Generated Keys' without
having to use JDBC to do so.  This capability is often used to access what
many DBMSs refer to as a Row ID of a just inserted or updated row.  And
while SQL/Foundation doesn't standardize a Row ID, the facility would have
utility by allowing access to what SQL/Foundation refers to as 'Identity
columns' or 'Generated columns'.
</para>

